:ruby
  PageHeader = import("/components/PageHeader.haml")
  DocsPage = import("/components/DocsPage.haml")
  DocsSection = import("/components/DocsSection.haml")

%DocsPage
  %PageHeader{
    kicker: "Plugin Reference",
    title: "Asset Plugins",
    summary: "SvgPlugin and ImagePlugin turn imported media into content-hashed browser assets with runtime-safe metadata."
  }

  %DocsSection{ title: "SvgPlugin" }
    :markdown
      `SvgPlugin` emits SVG assets and returns metadata with `src`, `width`, `height`, and `content_type`. Width and height come from the SVG element when available, or from the `viewBox` when they can be inferred.

      ```ruby
      Logo = import("./logo.svg")
      ```

  %DocsSection{ title: "ImagePlugin" }
    :markdown
      `ImagePlugin` emits raster source assets, generated default images, and generated variants. Imports can request widths, output formats, sizes, and quality.

      ```ruby
      Photo = import("./photo.jpg?width=320,640&format=webp&quality=82")
      ```

      Ruby imports return immutable `ImageMetadata` and `ImageVariant` values with `src`, dimensions, `content_type`, `aspect_ratio`, and variant-specific metadata. `ImageMetadata` also provides `variants`, `srcset`, and `sizes`. SVG imports return the corresponding immutable `SvgMetadata` value. Generated image work is queued as CPU-bound asset generation.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Cache Behavior" }
    :markdown
      Generated assets are content-hashed and can be written as they complete during build output. Existing generated files can be skipped when their output path is already present.

%title= "Asset Plugins"
